Task 2 -----> Create the ChatApp
    Flow:
            Client ---->  GenAIApp  ---->  LLMmodel

    issue : looses the context
    Sol: we can store the history somewhere , and we pass history with the client message(LLM does not store anything)

    Roles:
    System Role : As an LLM what are your roles and responsibilities(It has high priority than the user role).
    User Role : We, who wants to talk to the LLM models.
    Assistant Role : LLM model itself. The replies from llm comes under Assistant role.
    So, will store the messages like this:
        User ---> Hi, My name is Anany!
        Assistant ---> Hi Anany!

    Now, we started storing the context.

    Issue : Someone can ask irrelevant question. Want to reply only relevant ones.
        Proposed sol : In the very starting, we can add the prompt in the history that you are this and do not entertain irrelevant questions.
            But,there are 2 issues: we need to pass the long prompt with every message and someone can trick it using some good prompt
            because both have same priority(our prompt and user message, because we are passing the prompt as user message).
        Implemented sol : Use System PromptI

Context Window(input + output token) : Data in a single prompt

    Issue : Since, the history we are storing grows and we are passing that to the llm with every message. Hence, a lot of tokens
    are going to get consumed in reading the history.
        Proposed sol : Summarize the history except last few messages. But this is also not a full proof plan as with this
            way also our llm might hallucinate. We also have better options available like RAG and memory which we will discuss later.


Hallucination : LLM sounds confident even when they are wrong
    Cannot eliminate(because it is based on probability) it, but can be reduced using RAG, guardrails, Memory, Validations etc.